{#-
    Strength of a new password, in real time (app.js), and the requirements of PasswordRules, each marked as met or
    not. Without JavaScript, the requirements stay listed as a hint. The strength is estimated like the server does
    (PasswordStrength of Symfony): what the meter shows is what the form will accept.
    Variables: input_id (password field), confirm_id (confirmation field, optional), email_input_id (field holding the
    email address, optional) or email (address already known, optional), min_length.
-#}
{%- set meter_id = input_id ~ '-meter' -%}
<div class="password-meter" id="{{ meter_id }}" data-password-meter data-for="{{ input_id }}"
     data-min-length="{{ min_length }}"
     {%- if confirm_id ?? null %} data-confirm="{{ confirm_id }}"{% endif %}
     {%- if email_input_id ?? null %} data-email-input="{{ email_input_id }}"{% elseif email ?? null %} data-email="{{ email }}"{% endif %}
     data-level-0="{{ 'Très faible'|trans }}" data-level-1="{{ 'Faible'|trans }}" data-level-2="{{ 'Moyenne'|trans }}"
     data-level-3="{{ 'Forte'|trans }}" data-level-4="{{ 'Très forte'|trans }}"
     data-met="{{ 'respectée'|trans }}" data-unmet="{{ 'non respectée'|trans }}">
    <div class="password-strength" data-password-strength hidden>
        <span class="strength-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="strength-fill" data-strength-fill data-level="0"></span></span>
        <p class="password-strength-label" aria-live="polite">{{ 'Robustesse :'|trans }} <strong data-strength-label>{{ 'Très faible'|trans }}</strong></p>
    </div>
    <p class="password-rules-title" id="{{ meter_id }}-rules">{{ 'Le mot de passe doit :'|trans }}</p>
    <ul class="password-rules" aria-labelledby="{{ meter_id }}-rules">
        <li data-rule="length"><span class="rule-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ 'faire au moins %count% caractères ;'|trans({'%count%': min_length}) }}<span class="visually-hidden" data-rule-state></span></li>
        {% if (email_input_id ?? null) or (email ?? null) %}
        <li data-rule="email"><span class="rule-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ 'ne pas contenir votre adresse e-mail ;'|trans }}<span class="visually-hidden" data-rule-state></span></li>
        {% endif %}
        <li data-rule="strength"><span class="rule-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ 'être assez imprévisible : robustesse « Moyenne » au moins (une phrase de plusieurs mots est idéale) ;'|trans }}<span class="visually-hidden" data-rule-state></span></li>
        {% if confirm_id ?? null %}
        <li data-rule="match"><span class="rule-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ 'être saisi deux fois à l\'identique.'|trans }}<span class="visually-hidden" data-rule-state></span></li>
        {% endif %}
    </ul>
    <p class="hint">{{ 'À l\'envoi, Patrimeter vérifie aussi qu\'il ne figure pas dans des fuites de données connues (de façon anonyme : seul le début de son empreinte part).'|trans }}</p>
</div>
